Fix a crash when leaving SYSTEM SETTINGS

OptionListComponent::getSelected() does selected.at(0) guarded only by an
assert, which NDEBUG removes in a release build. An option list built
from a platform enumeration helper can legitimately be empty, and
GuiMenu's GPU governor save function calls getSelected() outside its
changed() guard - so opening SYSTEM SETTINGS and pressing back threw
std::out_of_range out of a UI callback. TRYCATCH in the main loop
rethrows it, so the frontend aborts:

  ERROR InputManager::parseEvent Exception vector::_M_range_check:
        __n (which is 0) >= this->size() (which is 0)
  terminate called after throwing an instance of 'std::exception'

Return a default-constructed value when nothing is selected, and give
the GPU governor list the same fallback entry the CPU list above it
already has - selectFirstItem() cannot select anything from an empty
list.

--- a/es-core/src/components/OptionListComponent.h	2026-09-20 19:55:33.484971179 -0400
+++ b/es-core/src/components/OptionListComponent.h	2026-09-20 19:55:33.509002354 -0400
@@ -345,7 +345,14 @@
 	{
 		assert(mMultiSelect == false);
 		auto selected = getSelectedObjects();
-		assert(selected.size() == 1);
+		// An option list can legitimately end up with nothing selected:
+		// menus build these from enumeration helpers that may return
+		// nothing on a given platform. The size assert above is compiled
+		// out by NDEBUG in a release build, so .at(0) then threw
+		// std::out_of_range out of a UI callback - and TRYCATCH in the
+		// main loop rethrows, taking the whole frontend down.
+		if (selected.empty())
+			return T();
 		return selected.at(0);
 	}
 
--- a/es-app/src/guis/GuiMenu.cpp	2026-09-20 19:55:33.485531286 -0400
+++ b/es-app/src/guis/GuiMenu.cpp	2026-09-20 19:55:33.509752720 -0400
@@ -2015,7 +2015,14 @@
 	}
 	
 	if (!selectedGpuGovernorFound)
-		optionsGpuGovernors->selectFirstItem(); // Preselect 'default' 
+	{
+		// Same fallback the CPU governor list above uses. selectFirstItem()
+		// cannot help when the list is empty, which is what happens when
+		// get_available_gpu_governors is unavailable - and this menu's save
+		// function calls getSelected() outside its changed() guard, so
+		// merely opening SYSTEM SETTINGS and backing out was fatal.
+		optionsGpuGovernors->add(selectedGpuGovernor, selectedGpuGovernor, true);
+	}
 
 	s->addWithLabel(_("DEFAULT GPU SCALING GOVERNOR"), optionsGpuGovernors);
 	s->addSaveFunc([selectedGpuGovernor, optionsGpuGovernors]
